# Doc sync after implementations

Whenever you implement or change product behavior, setup, APIs, UX, architecture, or tests in this repo, update the relevant docs in the same change set (or immediately after):

1. `README.md` — repo overview, features, workflow, status, troubleshooting
2. `frontend/README.md` — Flutter layout, UX notes, widget tests
3. `frontend/integration_test/README.md` — E2E suites, harness, how to run
4. `ARCHITECTURE.md` — when modules, ports, APIs, transport, milestones, or folder layout change (mark shipped vs planned)

## What to update

- New or removed user-facing features → Features / UX notes / typical workflow / module catalog
- Setup, ports, env vars, dart-defines → Prerequisites / Configuration / Running
- New or renamed tests → test tables and suite lists
- New backend routes or services → ARCHITECTURE API + folder structure + milestone status
- Terminology or chrome changes → match the UI copy users see
- Do **not** leave the default Flutter starter text in `frontend/README.md`

## What not to do

- Do not invent unreleased milestones as “Done”
- Do not replace ARCHITECTURE design principles with a pure runbook — keep ports/events/plugins as the north star and mark status honestly
- Skip doc edits only for pure refactors with zero user/dev/architecture-facing change
